+## §6 POLLS (STATELESS)
+
+### §6.1 Canonical messages and candidate proof
+
+Concrete wire proposal for approval: u8 version=2, u8 kind (0=POLL,1=REPLY_MATCH,2=REPLY,3=REPLY_DIFF), then tip_context[32] on every message. This new version prevents confusing old session messages with polls. Integers are u64LE unless stated, lengths canonical CompactSize, no trailing bytes. poll_id is nonzero and strictly increases without reuse per node; exhaustion is a local error. Exclusions are strictly ascending nonzero IDs. Fully validate lengths, bounds, integer arithmetic and grammar before allocating message-owned collections. Incompatible versions do not enter protocol handling.
+
+```
+POLL: poll_id, nonce[16], root[32], set_size, mode:u8, n,
+      m:CompactSize, cells[m]
+REPLY_MATCH: poll_id, proof[16]
+REPLY: poll_id, root_vote[32], set_size,
+       exclusion_count:CompactSize, exclusions[exclusion_count],
+       m:CompactSize, cells[m]
+REPLY_DIFF: poll_id, root_vote[32], set_size,
+            exclusion_count:CompactSize, exclusions[exclusion_count],
+            missing_count:CompactSize, missing[missing_count],
+            wanted_count:CompactSize, wanted[wanted_count]
+```
+
+POLL mode=0 requests prefix [0,n); mode=1 requests probe {0} union {2^k−1 <= set_size}, k>=1, sorted/deduplicated and clipped to the shared cell cap by retaining the lowest requested indices. POLL’s basis is its send-time set_size, not a separate wire field. Prefix n>=1; probe n=0. REPLY is always a dense prefix [0,m), including after a probe, and carries neither mode nor basis_size. There is no redundant REPLY correlation metadata; peer, poll_id and tip context correlate it with the current slot.
+
+set_size is own distinct admitted |R| at send/reply time, not |R union Pending|. POLL carries the poller's own R encoding at exactly the requested indices: prefix[0,n) or the clipped probe set. Its cells,root and set_size are computed from the same state. For prefix POLL m=n; for probe m is exactly the prescribed clipped index count. The receiver validates those identities and cell structure before any Ref-dependent decode. For fallback prefix REPLY, m=min(max_symbols_per_reply,max(2*n,S(abs(set_size_r−set_size_q)))). No successful-decode S(Delta) reply-cell floor remains: success sends plain IDs instead. For a probe,let h be the largest probe index actually sent;fallback REPLY is prefix[0,m),m=min(max_symbols_per_reply,max(2*(h+1),S(abs(set_size_r−set_size_q)))). Use checked/saturating arithmetic before allocation. No partial ID lists,leftover residuals or bitmaps are sent in fallback replies. At the cap the prefix cannot grow further;no unconditional growth beyond the cap is claimed. Cells, root_vote, set_size and full exclusions=R_ID minus candidate IDs are all computed from one current responder state during the serialized call. The responder keeps no poll bookkeeping and answers every well-formed POLL; generic rate limiting belongs to the host.
+
+If responder’s candidate root equals the POLL root, send REPLY_MATCH without decoding POLL cells; structural validation still applies. Otherwise peel the POLL once against responder raw R_ID, not Pending, captured at call entry. Do not retain or rescue inbound POLL cells. On success, if the complete DIFF fits the message limit, send missing=negative decoded IDs (responder-only) and wanted=positive decoded IDs (poller-only), each strictly ascending, nonzero and disjoint. The responder fetches its eligible positive items from the poller through ordinary FetchBody with the existing Pending reservation, binding and alternate-donor lifecycle. wanted describes absence for item votes; it is not a body request and triggers no body-send host action. Ordinary incomplete inbound positives use that same bounded fetch path. An explicit contradiction discards all effects of the inbound attempt before fallback. A decode never inserts R. Response cells, root_vote, set_size and exclusions refer to one coherent responder state.
+
+On ordinary incomplete decode or explicit peel contradiction, fall back to REPLY with cells using the existing sizing rule; no REPLY_DIFF is emitted. Peel-derived faults are silent; structural cell faults remain reportable. Partial positives from an ordinary incomplete inbound attempt follow normal fetch rules. An explicit contradiction discards ALL effects of that attempt before building fallback REPLY. If successful decoding produces a complete REPLY_DIFF exceeding the message limit, send fallback REPLY cells instead; never truncate or fragment the ID lists. Inbound decoding uses raw R so normal Pending assumptions from other peers cannot be used as its reference. For candidate IDs x, proof is LE64(XOR SipHash-2-4(nonce,0x00||LE64(x))) followed by LE64(XOR SipHash-2-4(nonce,0x01||LE64(x))). Decode nonce's first/second eight bytes as little-endian k0/k1. Hash each distinct candidate ID once, regardless of body bucket size; empty XOR=0. Nonces come from the core's seeded RNG (proposed two consecutive u64 draws serialized LE). All polls of a round are sent at round start from one state. Keep ONE round capture: admitted raw IDs with admission incarnation and candidate bit, plus Pending IDs live at round start with their live item-lifetime identity, at most M+P records total. No body handles or per-slot copies are retained. Each slot stores its 16-byte expected proof over captured W and points at that capture. Only captured item lifetimes still live at scoring time receive this round’s observations; matching Pending admission preserves its lifetime and eligibility, while loss of support or removal/readmission does not. Items first appearing after capture get no votes this round. Release the capture at round end or tip reset. A delayed poll shares the capture only if the captured admitted/candidate/Pending state remains unchanged; otherwise defer it to the next round. Never create a second capture. Verify REPLY_MATCH against the stored proof even if current own root has changed. Mismatch still causes inconsistent_reply and abstention; do not discard a valid old-root MATCH merely because a body was admitted meanwhile. Candidate proof is algebraic set evidence, not authentication of bodies or identities.
+
+The poller keeps fixed current-round slots (peer,poll_id,nonce,n,mode,send-time |R|,sent root,sent time,expected proof[16],shared round-capture reference,answer status). Correlated duplicates cannot contribute twice. Stale/unknown context or connection generations cannot mutate current evidence. Discard late replies entirely: no decoding, fetching, sizing, evidence or votes. No past-round slots are retained.
+
+
+REPLY_DIFF is a complete reconstruction with no cell peeling or retention; its lists remain unauthenticated peer assertions. W_j=((round capture raw R minus wanted) union missing) minus peer exclusions. Start from captured raw R, including locally excluded IDs. For a captured Pending ID absent from captured raw R, the peer holds it exactly when it occurs in missing; use this reconstruction for all eligible captured lifetimes. Post-capture items receive no observation. Removal/readmission invalidates old-incarnation observations; matching live Pending admission preserves its state and eligibility. The poller starts ordinary FetchBody for eligible missing items, deduplicating concurrent in-flight/awaiting operations and preserving alternate-donor retry. wanted triggers no fetch or body-send action at the poller. Admission remains host-authoritative. Record Delta_hat_start=|missing|+|wanted| and Delta_hat_now=|missing minus current Ref|+|wanted intersect current R| at reply-processing entry, before Pending effects. These are exact counts of the specified lists, not authenticated holdings. DIFF supplies the normal exact sizing sample and complete per-item observations.
+
+Validate list lengths, strictly ascending nonzero IDs, disjoint missing/wanted, wanted membership in captured raw R and missing absence from captured raw R, and set_size=sent_set_size+missing_count−wanted_count with checked arithmetic. The asserted peer raw set is (captured raw R minus wanted) union missing; its cardinality must equal set_size and its exclusions must be a subset. Exclusion and complete-message bounds apply. Reject an internally inconsistent DIFF before any fetch or observation effect, using captured raw R rather than current R or Pending. This checks the assertion’s internal consistency and does not authenticate the peer’s holdings.
+
+wanted only describes peer absence for voting. Body transfers in both directions use ordinary FetchBody from the node that decoded a positive item: the responder fetches positives from the POLL, and the poller fetches missing from DIFF or fallback decoding. No body-send action or new receive-token protocol exists. Duplicate/stale replies cannot duplicate operations. Fallback decoding causes no automatic back-propagation; a node discovers items through its own polls and existing fetch path.
+
+### §6.2 One-call decoding
+
+Capture Ref=own R_ID union Pending at reply-processing entry and keep it fixed as input for the entire call. Decode received cells minus Ref's encoding at their indices; every later rescue attempt similarly captures the current Ref at its start. The peeler's private working reference changes as it peels, not the captured Ref. Success means all residuals zero. Decoded items are algebraically consistent, never authenticated holdings. FetchBody and host validation remain the only authority for admission.
+
+After the arrival peel completes, eligible decoded positive items may start bounded fetches and thereby enter Pending. No prefix continuation occurs. W_j=((Ref union decoded_positive) minus decoded_negative) minus exclusions_j describes a complete reconstruction only when no residual remains. Record this round’s item observations from the arrival outcome under §8, before later rescue attempts can discover more items. An item preference or counter alone never cancels a fetch or creates an epoch rejection mark. Partial positives still use the normal fetch path. Successful arrival replies release cell workspace after discovery/observations; ordinary incomplete replies retain indices, exclusions and ONE invariant residual array for dissemination/rescue. Core retains no second raw-cell array. Raw cells can be reconstructed as residual+encode(current Ref); the harness separately owns wire bytes. Nothing is retained across round end or tip cancellation. Explicit contradictions discard the reply under the existing nonpunitive policy.
+
+For each retained reply, invariant residual=raw cells−encode(current Ref) at its indices. A Ref membership gain/loss applies exactly one signed contribution at the item's scheduled indices in every retained reply. Update only net Ref membership: Pending-to-R or R-to-Pending transitions preserving membership have no delta. Admissions, removals, Pending changes, fetch failures and probation use this same rule. A decoded item never inserts R and never directly changes the invariant buffer; only the Ref change it actually causes does so.
+
+Each peel attempt copies the invariant residual into ONE transient working buffer of at most max_symbols_per_reply cells, peels that copy, then discards it. Charge the buffer within decode workspace. Never retain private peel subtractions as invariant residuals. Capture Ref at attempt start for W_j and audit; after peel, apply eligible fetch/Pending effects. Partial positives follow the same live-fetch rules; they do not authenticate bodies.
+
+Maintain a dirty set ordered by poll order. A Ref change marks retained replies with touched scheduled indices. Repeatedly attempt the smallest dirty reply until none is dirty. A successful rescue reconstructs the peer raw/candidate view against that attempt’s Ref, discovers donors and fetches eligible items, then releases cell workspace. Rescue contributes no new item observations that round: neither decoded later items nor newly inferred shared items replace arrival abstention. This includes dirty-set attempts caused within the same API call after the first arrival peel. Already eligible arrival observations remain governed by their captured lifetime and the existing validity/discard rules. Ordinary failure leaves the reply retained and clean; contradictions follow §6.6. Cascading Ref additions can dirty earlier replies; choose the smallest dirty poll order next.
+
+Arrival observations use the existing bounded round-evidence records keyed to captured item lifetimes and selected peers. Record at most one outcome per selected peer/item; later rescue does not update it. Ordinary lifetime/validity filters still apply at scoring. No per-reply cell-index evidence buffer or extra evidence-only peel is retained or run. Capture/evidence storage is released at round end or tip reset and actual capacities remain charged under §6.5.
+
+No work cap and no proportionality claim. A retained reply is re-peeled only after a Ref change touches its indices. Within the cascade of one call, Ref gains at most P new Pending entries and an ID cannot re-enter Pending in that call. Assert attempts per call<=retained-reply bound*(1+Ref changes in the call), conservatively using K as the reply bound, without terminating at a runtime cap. Record residual-update touches separately from actual re-peel steps/attempts and rescued replies. No dirty reply remains when the call finishes. Admission and root changes do not abandon the round. Keep eligible item evidence and update retained residuals for net Ref changes, including admission/removal. There is no separate root-confidence state or root-change scoring veto. Tip/generation reset still cancels the round. Rescues use current Ref for dissemination; item observation eligibility and values come from the arrival outcome and the corresponding captured lifetime.
+
+Sizing Delta_hat_now and Delta_hat_start are captured only at first processing, using its pre-peel bitmap and original attempt's lower bound; later attempts create no new samples and never rewrite earlier ones. The first peel counts as one attempt. A residual-delta audit record is per (Ref item,retained reply) pair, not per touched cell. Full-observation tests record the complete cascade in observation-owned growable storage (§10); audit allocation failure is a test failure, not a protocol ResourceLimit or an atomic-reservation requirement. Do not reserve a worst-case audit envelope. Protocol reservations and the attempt/no-dirty assertions remain mandatory.
+
+
+Inbound POLLs disseminate items only; their reference is own R_ID, distinct from the R_ID union Pending reference used when decoding received REPLY cells. They supply no batch vote, no per-transaction vote and no Delta_hat_now/Delta_hat_start sizing sample: the responder did not select who polls it, and adversaries can poll at will. Use the existing transient working buffer for one attempt, charge its inbound per-attempt signed-claim bound2*M within the existing per-call claim accounting and observation attempt counters, then release all POLL-cell workspace. Inbound-triggered fetches use the existing P union reservation. No inbound poll slot is retained. Pending additions from an inbound POLL are ordinary Ref changes: update retained outbound residuals and run normal dirty-order rescue. These rescues disseminate items but do not create or upgrade this round’s item observations. Inbound polls themselves never gain evidence eligibility or sizing samples.
+
+### §6.3 Adaptive sizing and frozen S(d)
+
+A timely REPLY_DIFF supplies uncensored start and now samples defined in §6.1. A fallback REPLY means either inbound decode did not succeed or a complete DIFF exceeded the message limit; apply the existing approximate estimator and growth rule to its cells. Every timely processed REPLY with cells records which residual cells are zero BEFORE peeling. Exclude index0 from the likelihood because p0=1; a zero symbol0 is used in the explicit zero-estimate branch below. For i>=1 use p_i=2/(i+2) and the model P(empty at i)=(1−p_i)^Delta. This is an independence approximation: schedule cells are correlated and mixed-sign cancellation is treated as negligible. Call the result the approximate maximum-likelihood estimate, not an exact MLE.
+
+Let L=max(number of distinct items decoded from this reply,abs(raw symbol0 count minus reference symbol0 count)). Maximize over integer Delta>=L:
+
+`sum_empty Delta*ln(1−p_i) + sum_nonempty ln(1−(1−p_i)^Delta)`.
+
+The stated objective is unimodal; search integer Delta in[L,2*M+P] with smaller-Delta tie breaking and stable log evaluation. If the maximizer would lie above the domain, record a censored result at L; never perform unbounded search. If all received nonzero-index cells are pre-peel empty and symbol0 residual is zero, Delta_hat=0. If no nonzero-index cell is pre-peel empty, record a censored estimate with lower bound L. For probe{0} with no nonzero-index cells, zero symbol0 residual gives Delta_hat=0; otherwise censor at L. The estimate is an approximation even on hostile input and never authenticates a set. Censored samples enter request selection at L; no floating-point estimates are rounded into different counts silently.
+
+Compute two estimates per reply. Delta_hat_now uses the Ref captured at reply entry and sizes the next round. Delta_hat_start applies the same estimator after adding back the effect of items that entered Pending/Ref since round start, bounded by P, solely for estimation; it determines the next-height ratio. Neither estimate can mutate the peeler reference or produce extra body/evidence actions. Maintain a per-round list of additions to Ref still present at processing time, bounded by P. R/Pending transitions that leave membership unchanged are not recorded; removals drop the ID. Add back each listed item's encoding to the residual to undo its Ref subtraction. Delta_hat_start uses L=max(items decoded in the first attempt,absolute symbol0 count difference after add-back). If the list would exceed P, disable start estimation for the rest of that round and use Delta_hat_now as its ratio sample instead; no penalty or abandonment. Charge the P-record list explicitly; no cross-round change log.
+
+The frozen table stores quantiles5%,10%,...,95% and100% of needed prefix length at each grid d. Let F_d(n) be the conservative step CDF defined below. P_hat(n)=mean_i F_{Delta_hat_now_i}(n). Candidate n values are the union of stored quantile lengths and S for current samples, each capped at max_symbols_per_reply: at most21*D values before deduplication. Minimize n/P_hat(n), ties to smaller n; for this cost comparison, positive n divided by zero is +infinity, so if every candidate has P_hat(n)=0 choose the smallest candidate and then apply the existing growth and cap rules. No usable samples with an existing prefix retain that prefix subject to the doubling floor below; without a prefix or usable round1 history, use the initial probe. A round with REPLY_DIFF samples sizes the next request from those exact samples using this normal estimator, even if every reply is REPLY_DIFF; n may shrink. Only a round with no sizing samples (only MATCH or silence) keeps the previous request n. The doubling triggers below are unchanged. Censored samples enter at their lower bound L. Sort a censored sample above an uncensored sample of equal value when taking the upper median. Censoring triggers prefix growth, never a return to probe mode once a prefix exists.
+
+
+Censored/zero-decode escalation: remember the previous prefix request within the epoch for the conditional doubling floor; it is not an unconditional lower bound on later requests. Zero-decode doubling requires at least one fallback REPLY with cells, none of those replies succeeding on arrival/rescue, and no REPLY_DIFF success in that round. A REPLY_DIFF counts as success. Independently, a censored upper-median sizing sample triggers doubling. If either trigger holds and a prior prefix exists, choose n_next=min(cap,max(estimator_n,2*n_previous)), with checked/saturating arithmetic; the estimator may choose more,never less. A round with only MATCH or silence and no samples keeps previous n; a round with REPLY_DIFF samples uses the normal estimator and may shrink n when neither unchanged doubling trigger applies. No empty/no-cell round is called a zero-decode failure.
+
+Use the exponential probe only when this epoch has no prior prefix and no usable round1 history. For the first prefix after a probe: if its upper-median sample is censored or unusable, n=(largest probe index actually sent)+1, subject to the existing max_symbols_per_reply cap; otherwise use the estimator. This span is the prescribed transition operand, not authentication that all positions contain differences. Once the first prefix exists, apply the doubling rule from there and never return to probe mode within the epoch. This replaces the reported prefix/probe livelock without a new tuning constant.
+
+First height probes. For new-height round1 apply the same empirical argmin to previous-height round1 samples individually scaled by |R|_now/|R|_then and rounded up. The scaled samples use the same upper-median censor ordering; they do not authorize returning to probe mode once a prefix exists. Previous |R|=0 or absent usable history permits a probe only when this epoch has no prior prefix. Record end-round1 |R| and r=median Delta_hat_start/|R| as a diagnostic; the sample-by-sample scaling, not a single median substitution, controls request sizing. Reorg/disconnect height transition uses available saved round1 information, otherwise probes.
+
+Retain at most D_max=1024 records in each of two banks: current-round samples and reusable round1 samples. Consume previous-height round1 bank when sizing the new round1, then overwrite it with new round1 observations. Bounds do not shrink when current D changes. Clear ordinary current-round samples at boundary; retain the specified round1 history only. No per-peer probe bit; late replies are discarded entirely.
+
+The frozen sizing table is a reproducible empirical distribution table independent of M. d=0 gives prefix length1 for every quantile. For positive d generate2000 trials of d distinct uniform nonzero IDs, equiprobable signs, independent reference peeler. Grid={0..64} union {round(64*(11/10)^k)} through d_max=4096, including deduplicated endpoint4096; use nearest-integer half-up grid rounding. SplitMix64 seed0x534E4F5753544F52 supplies successive ID outputs, rejecting zero/duplicates; accepted ID's sign is the low bit of the next output. Generator cap=floor((2MiB−100)/28)=74894; cap-exhausted trials count as that cap.
+
+Store5%..95% in5% steps plus100%. Each quantile uses1-based order statistic ceil(q*N), N=2000. F_d(n) is the largest stored q whose quantile length<=n; below the5% quantile F=0, and at/above stored maximum F=1. Equal quantile lengths select the largest qualifying q. Between d grid points use the next larger grid d for F (conservative). For d>4096, scale every stored quantile length by d/4096 and round up before evaluating F. S(d) is the stored50% quantile,1-based rank1000 of2000 (superseding the former upper-middle convention). S retains linear interpolation between grid points, rounded up, and its linear extension beyond4096; F retains the next-larger-grid rule. S remains the responder floor. Runtime reply cap applies after S and to candidate request lengths. Freeze generator,seed,table and digest together only after approval.
+
+Validation: known Delta in{10,50,150,500},1000 trials each, prefix length S(Delta). Mean Delta_hat/Delta in[0.9,1.1], p90 in[0.7,1.4]. Include censored samples at lower bound L; p90 is nearest-rank over all1000 ratios, report censor count separately. Do not retune the estimator or seeds to force success.
+
+### §6.4 Body outcomes — retained cleanup contract
+
+The earlier cleanup contract is translated where session state no longer exists. Live Pending carries the §8 Snowball item state. Replace every former scalar-confidence transfer with an item-state lifetime transfer; matching admission preserves its whole Snowball state, including preference, counters, previous success and FINAL. Admission does not force preference in; FINAL-out remains out.
+
+On invalid/matched for outstanding unadmitted x: remove x from Pending,probation,donor and transient assumption records, mark rejected for this height, and emit PeerMisbehaved(invalid_body). Rejected IDs are never fetched or accepted this height, including the conservative collision limitation in§3. No retained session/reference model exists.
+
