+For each nonfinal captured item, count yes and no from these eligible observations. A round succeeds for IN if yes>=alpha, succeeds for OUT if no>=alpha, and has no success otherwise. Abstentions do not count toward either side, but never reduce alpha. Fewer than alpha usable observations cannot cause success. For K>0, alpha>K/2. Since each selected peer contributes at most one yes/no outcome for an item and yes+no<=K, IN and OUT can never both succeed, including beta_adv=0 and even K.
